From 80dc1ba12cf1c372ff038fcba45be8d030d10feb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:56:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fp8-decode: block-FP8 GEMV and split-K for decode-sized dense
 GEMMs

Faster block-FP8 dense GEMMs for decode-sized inputs. With up to four
rows, `w8a8_block_fp8_matmul_triton` runs a Triton GEMV
(`fp8_block_gemv.py`) that steps K over several scale groups at a time.
With up to 16 rows and no tuned config for the shape, the Triton matmul
uses a split-K tiling.

Numerics: Not bit-identical when on: the same FP8 operands summed in a
different fp32 order (GEMV, split-K). Prefill shapes are unchanged.

Prerequisites: none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
---
 python/sglang/kernels/ops/gemm/fp8_kernel.py  |  51 +++++-
 .../ops/quantization/fp8_block_gemv.py        | 172 ++++++++++++++++++
